{number: 88}
{title: My Jesus, As Thou Wilt!}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
My [Eb] Jesus, as Thou [Ab] wilt!
O [Eb] may Thy [Bb7] will be [Eb] mine!
Into Thy hand of [Ab] love
I [Eb] would my [Bb7] all re-[Eb] sign;
Through [Bb7] sorrow or through [Eb] joy,
Conduct me [Bb7] as Thine [Eb] own,
And help me still to [Ab] say,
My [Eb] Lord, Thy [Bb7] will be [Eb] done!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
My [Eb] Jesus, as Thou [Ab] wilt!
Though [Eb] seen through [Bb7] many a [Eb] tear,
Let not my star of [Ab] hope
Grow [Eb] dim or [Bb7] disap-[Eb] pear;
Since [Bb7] Thou on earth hast [Eb] wept,
And sorrowed [Bb7] oft a-[Eb] lone,
If I must weep with [Ab] Thee,
My [Eb] Lord, Thy [Bb7] will be [Eb] done!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
My [Eb] Jesus, as Thou [Ab] wilt!
All [Eb] shall be [Bb7] well for [Eb] me;
Each changing future [Ab] scene
I [Eb] gladly [Bb7] trust with [Eb] Thee:
Straight [Bb7] to my home a-[Eb] bove
I travel [Bb7] calmly [Eb] on,
And sing in life or [Ab] death,
My [Eb] Lord, Thy [Bb7] will be [Eb] done!
{end_of_verse}
